# Where the app finds the route handlers in apps/web. Required — unlike the web
# app, which just talks to its own origin, the device has to be told.
#
# Local development: your machine's LAN address, not localhost. A phone running
# the app resolves "localhost" to itself, so the request never leaves the
# handset. Run `npm run dev` in apps/web and use the address Expo prints for the
# dev server, on port 3000:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=http://192.168.1.20:3000
#
# An iOS simulator or Android emulator on the same machine is the exception:
#   iOS simulator      http://localhost:3000
#   Android emulator   http://10.0.2.2:3000
#
# Production: the Render URL.
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://cinesync.onrender.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=
